context:BENCH.harness:
Layout: bench/ inside the repo holds the spec, the schemas and the scorers. bench/corpus/fetch.py downloads corpora into $OHB_CACHE, outside the source tree, and verifies each against corpus.lock.toml (URL, tag, SHA, sha256, license, tier). Oracles live in bench/oracles/java (Gradle project: semanticdb-javac, an ASM CFG dumper, SootUp/OPAL call graphs, a JVM trace agent, a JCG adapter) and bench/oracles/py (path counts, layout metrics, PlantUML/mermaid/XMI validators). Competitor wrappers go in bench/adapters/<tool>. bench/score computes P/R/F1 with bootstrap CIs, and McNemar tests for paired tool comparisons. benches/ holds criterion or divan benches and gungraun (formerly iai-callgrind) instruction counts, and baselines/vN/*.json is committed. The engine must add 'openheart export --format ohb-json'.

Reproducibility: rust-toolchain.toml, cargo build --release --locked, a Docker image pinned by digest, and pinned JDK 21, PlantUML and mermaid-cli. Every results.jsonl row records suite version, corpus SHA, tool commit, CPU, kernel and governor.

CI tiers:
- PR, under 15 minutes: golden IR and proptest; JCG, PointerBench and SecuriBench subsets; BDD oracles; diagram validity; gungraun instruction counts; tier-S correctness; artifact bytes.
- Nightly, on a dedicated runner with isolated, fixed-frequency cores: tiers M-L, the full suites, XCorpus recall, P-MARt and layout.
- Weekly and at release: tiers XL-XXL plus competitor re-runs.

A run fails on any of:
- any oracle or invariant violation;
- any previously passing JCG or PointerBench case that now fails;
- an F1 drop of more than 0.5 pp, or one outside the bootstrap CI;
- instruction counts up more than 2%;
- wall time flagged by a Bencher t-test (upper boundary 0.99), or by github-action-benchmark with alert at 110% and fail at 120% (its default is 200%);
- peak RSS up more than 5%, bytes per LOC up more than 2%, or query p99 up more than 10%.

Integrity: oracles are protected by CODEOWNERS and may not share lists with the engine. 30% of corpora are held out and scored only at release.

Publishing: a versioned 'OpenHeart Bench vN' page is generated from results.jsonl. Competitor rows are labelled 'published' or 'reproduced'. Raw outputs get a Zenodo DOI. A claims-lint CI step requires every number in the README to cite a result id. The SIGPLAN empirical-evaluation checklist is followed.
